omx-plugins (0.11.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Factory presets: 120 presets for the 19 plugins, installed with the
    omx-plugins package as files in /usr/share/omx/presets, one directory
    per plugin. The catalogue presets are checked against their measured
    figures through the DSP.
  * omx-plugins-dev also installs the test plugins' generated declaration
    headers, which hold the constants and CLAP id a test predicts from.
  * The compressor and de-esser level meters read their level through
    omx-dsp's omx_meter_level_db instead of a copy of their own. The readings
    are bit for bit the same.
  * Builds against omx-dsp >= 0.24.0 and omx-contract >= 2.16.0.
  * The oracles take their sample rates from omx-contract's
    OMX_ORACLE_FULL_RATES_* names.
  * The strip's cross-check declares the low-pass above 0.6 of Nyquist as a
    known gap and checks the rest.
  * The parameter, panel, CLAP extension and port group checks each have
    sabotage tests that must fail on a broken face.
  * A parallel make no longer races on the EQ default probe: each build makes
    its own copy and moves it into place.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000

omx-plugins (0.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every plugin over one kernel is described in omx-contract's own words: a
    descriptor file per plugin carries its identity, its controls with their
    symbols, names, groups, meanings and the definitions their travels are
    read from, its ports and its latency, and the declaration keeps only
    what the descriptor has no word for.
  * The built CLAP and LV2 faces are scanned as a host scans any plugin, and
    must state exactly what the descriptor says.
  * The panel description is laid out from a descriptor, so any plugin, ours
    or a scanned one, gets a panel; a LUFS or dBu level takes the threshold
    and ceiling roles.
  * omx transient is no longer drawn under the compressor's family: a
    declared family needs the meanings it stands on.
  * Builds against omx-contract >= 2.15.0 and omx-dsp >= 0.22.0, which ships
    the kernels' definitions; the build reads them from the contract
    directory through the omx-contract command.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

omx-plugins (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every meter is coherent: the plugins publish their meters through a
    ring of three copies, so a host never reads values from two different
    blocks.
  * omx comp reports its gain reduction and its input and output levels,
    and the de-esser its input and output levels.
  * omx pitch declares its units: semitones and cents are whole steps
    that a host shows as semitones and cents, and the mix as a percent.
  * The plugins use the meters header omx-clap-core installs instead of a
    copy of their own.
  * The first release that waits for plugin-qualify: every plugin is
    measured for real-time safety and must be rated suitable before any
    package is built, and the verdicts are kept with the release run.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

omx-plugins (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Library dependencies are a floor only, no ceiling: omx-dsp (>= 0.18.0,
    the first release the plugins build and pass `make test` against; 0.17.0
    does not link) and omx-contract (>= 2.11.0). tools/deps-check.sh fails
    on any upper bound.
  * The parameter-contract header names the LUFS unit (OMX_CLAP_UNIT_LUFS,
    0x103), which openmixer's MAIN loudness target travels in.

